# Cloak walkthrough with intentional drift in a few recorded blocks
# to demonstrate the word-level red/green/neutral diff display. All
# assertions still pass; drift is purely informational.

> west

  Cloakroom
  The walls of this tiny chamber were once lined with iron hooks,
  though only a single brass hook now remains. The exit is east.

? Cloakroom
? hooks


> hang cloak on hook

  (first taking it off)
  You put the velvet cloak on the small brass hook.

  [Your score has just gone up by one point.]

? velvet cloak


> east

  Foyer of the Opera House
  You are standing in a spacious red-and-gold hall with chandeliers.
  There are doorways south and west, and an entrance to the north.

? Foyer


> south

  Foyer Bar
  The bar, much rougher than you'd have guessed after the opulence
  of the foyer to the north, is completely empty. There seems to be
  some sort of message scrawled in the sawdust on the floor.

? message scrawled


> read message

  The message, neatly marked in the sawdust, reads...

      *** The End ***

  In that game you scored 2 out of a possible 2, in 5 turns.

  Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT or UNDO the last command?

? *** The End ***
